      ":question/problem": "Simplify $\\cos(x+210^\\circ)$ using $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$. Enter signed coefficients.\n\n{{field-1}} $\\sin x-$ {{field-2}} $\\cos x$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use $\\cos(u+v)=\\cos u\\cos v-\\sin u\\sin v$ with $u=x$ and $v=210^\\circ$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos(x+210^\\circ)&=\\cos x\\cos 210^\\circ-\\sin x\\sin 210^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\cos x\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)-\\sin x\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin x-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first blank is $\\frac{1}{2}$ and the second is $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$. The printed minus sign means the second entry is the negative of the cosine coefficient: $-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)=- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$.",
